{
  "id": 507076059,
  "iid": 25781,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "portableapps: preserve plugins directory across upgrades",
  "description": "## What this does\n\nAdds a `[SpecialPaths]` `Plugins=` entry to `packaging/portableapps/appinfo.tmpl`, telling the PortableApps.com installer to preserve the global plugins directory (and its per-version subfolders) across upgrades instead of deleting it.\n\n## Why\n\nPer the PortableApps.com Format spec, `Plugins=` marks a directory as excluded from the installer's default \"wipe and replace\" upgrade behavior. Wireshark's template never set this, so every major-version upgrade of Wireshark Portable silently deletes the previous version's global plugins folder  including any custom/manually-added plugins, with no warning and no way to recover them.\n\n## Status\n\nSmall, low-risk config change. I have not yet tested it against an actual PortableApps.com build/upgrade cycle (no Windows/NSIS environment available). Opening as a draft for early feedback on the approach — happy to test the full upgrade scenario (old version + custom plugin + upgrade) if a maintainer confirms this is the right direction.\n\nFixes #15550",
  "state": "merged",
